WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.282 --> 00:00:05.060
- As a result of my
studies, I found a thread

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.560
that the essence of
religion was compassion.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:11.760
That every single one of
the major world religions,

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.090
Judaism, Islam, Christianity,
Hinduism, Buddhism,

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:20.120
and Confucianism, they all
insisted on what's often

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.310
known as The Golden
Rule: Never treat others

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.810
as you would not like
to be treated yourself.

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:32.790
The wish was that we would
get a panel of activists,

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:36.470
and together we would craft a charter,

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:39.850
a brief statement reminding the world

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.800
that this is what religion is about.

00:00:44.747 --> 00:00:46.850
(melodic tones)

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:49.290
- They had a big idea to change the world.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:53.350
But they couldn't do it alone.

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:54.880
- So, my wish...
- So, my wish...

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:55.713
- I wish...

00:00:55.713 --> 00:00:56.546
- So now my wish...

00:00:56.546 --> 00:00:59.160
- And now, here's my wish...

00:01:04.766 --> 00:01:06.550
(voices yelling)

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:10.300
- Our nation seemed to
be crumbling by the day.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:13.880
And this should make us uncomfortable.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:15.970
We've all got huge problems in our cities.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:19.050
Problems of inequity and
cruelty and violence.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.540
So, what can we do?

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:26.360
What can we do to change things?

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.350
Every city has to be compassionate.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:30.010
And people often ask me, well, what should

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:32.610
a compassionate city be like?

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:35.610
And I said, “Well, a
compassionate city should

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.180
“be an uncomfortable city.”

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:42.270
One is Louisville,
Kentucky, where the mayor,

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:44.360
Greg Fischer, actually campaigned

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:46.360
on the idea of compassion.

00:01:49.384 --> 00:01:51.580
- When I announced
compassion as a city value,

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:53.120
it got a lot of attention.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:57.750
A city is a platform for
human potential to come alive.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.130
Compassion makes individuals stronger.

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:05.780
And it makes our cities stronger.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.890
- People just can't call
themselves a compassionate city

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:15.350
unless they've got a
practical course of action.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:18.960
- So the question then is,

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.770
how do you bring compassion alive?

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:23.070
How do you change the
culture of your city?

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:26.880
What if you could start at the beginning

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.080
of a young child's life?

00:02:29.193 --> 00:02:31.943
(slow hammering)

00:02:34.957 --> 00:02:39.624
(melodic tone chimes once and sustains)

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:51.340
- My name is Meghann Clem Mattingly.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:54.440
I am the Compassionate
School’s Project teacher.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.870
Compassion is a very teachable thing.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:58.830
OK.

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:01.380
I see a lot of friends
who are lookin' ready.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:04.570
Every CSP class begins
with calming and focusing.

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:07.940
And then, we have some
sort of core practice,

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:10.020
that we're doing, whether we're talking

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:13.180
about self-awareness or
empathy-building skills.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:17.780
We are starting at the ground level.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:20.330
We are building that
foundation for our students

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:24.610
at age 5 and up to be more
compassionate citizens.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:27.137
Goodbye, Jeremy.

00:03:27.137 --> 00:03:28.505
- (yelling) No!

00:03:28.505 --> 00:03:29.590
Jeremy, look at Miss Mattingly.

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:31.200
- Just go, calm down, just go.

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:33.840
Jeremiah, we're gonna try harder to get

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.301
our self-regulation back, sir.

00:03:37.301 --> 00:03:39.094
- This is the second
reason I'm mad at my life.

00:03:39.094 --> 00:03:39.927
- Jeremiah, come here.

00:03:39.927 --> 00:03:41.230
I need you to tell me more about that.

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:42.210
Jeremiah, come here.

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:45.036
Anger or frustration,
which feeling was bringing?

00:03:45.036 --> 00:03:45.869
- Anger.

00:03:45.869 --> 00:03:46.810
- Anger, I can tell.

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:48.200
Look at your hands.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:51.000
So, before we talk about it,
can you calm yourself down?

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:53.693
No?

00:03:53.693 --> 00:03:54.526
It's hard to, isn’t it?

00:03:54.526 --> 00:03:56.921
So can you try to make
your hands look like mine?

00:03:56.921 --> 00:03:58.180
Nope.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:03:59.273
Can you try to let go of that?

00:03:59.273 --> 00:04:00.106
- Nn-nn.

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:02.710
- Look at your face, I see a smile there.

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:04.900
You're tryin' real hard
to hang on to that anger.

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:08.090
I see everyday these changes
happening in these students.

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:11.740
And I have all the hope in
the world that this project

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:14.130
will change our education.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:17.940
- We define compassion as
respect for each and every one

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:19.990
of our citizens, so that
their human potential

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:21.710
is flourishing, thriving.

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:30.740
- [Group of women speaking in
Unison] Grant me the serenity

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:33.700
to accept the things
that I can not change,

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:36.430
the courage to change
the things that I can,

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:38.330
and the wisdom to know the difference,

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:40.110
just for today.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:41.150
Keep comin' back.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:42.520
It works.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:44.595
- Hotel Louisville is a great
example of how to think about

00:04:44.595 --> 00:04:48.790
the whole system of getting
a person back on track.

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:52.640
So it's a shelter for
women and their families,

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:55.310
but it's also an operating hotel.

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:58.910
- Hotel Louisville is not
just a women's rehab facility.

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:01.280
It is a workforce program.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.620
We run the hotel.

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:04.550
We do all the jobs here.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:11.450
Every time that one of us has
our own individual skills,

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:14.090
it gives us a sense of responsibility.

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:16.930
Because we can put this on
our resumes when we leave.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:24.380
- I think the compassion
really comes from the girls

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:28.280
that are in the rehab,
because we depend on each

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:29.780
other a lot.

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:31.220
We need each other.

00:05:33.357 --> 00:05:37.774
(background women's voices talking)

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:44.680
If I was not here at Hotel
Louisville, I would be sittin'

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:46.200
in jail doin' my time.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:48.700
I was given that chance.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:51.320
And I wanna live, I wanna live life.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:56.610
- It lifts us all up
to say this is the kind

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:58.830
of city we are, and
this is the kind of city

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:00.320
we aspire to be.

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:02.520
And that any way we can help other cities,

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:04.550
and to take us to even greater heights,

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:05.660
is what we wanna do.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:08.410
It's this ripple effect.

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:10.310
We're not perfect as a city.

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:12.940
But, boy, we're workin'
to be better every day.

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:16.140
- Here you have a city,
which is doing great

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:17.540
things with compassion.

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:23.522
Cities and mayors are
going to play an important

00:06:23.522 --> 00:06:25.200
role as leaders of the future.

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:34.580
I'd like to see a thousand
compassionate cities

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:39.170
in the next decade that
remind the rest of the world

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:41.090
what our duty is.

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:45.340
Always treat all others as you'd

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:47.180
like to be treated yourself.

00:06:48.855 --> 00:06:51.022
(silence)

